+## Numerical formula alignment
+
+### Reproducible method and coverage
+
+The supplied results cover all seven chapters and are accepted without re-estimation. Method: `editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py`. It strips H1 headings and marked scene breaks, removes emphasis markers, excludes fenced system notices from sentence/readability calculations, treats each non-empty manuscript line as a written paragraph, and counts exact marked breaks. Sentences are split at terminal punctuation followed by whitespace and a capital/opening quote, with common abbreviations and ellipses protected. Syllables use a vowel-group heuristic with silent-e and `-le` adjustments; proper names and system terms use the same estimator and can bias Flesch results. There are no fenced system-notice words in this movement. The three placeholder lines remain prose and will cause a small metric change when replaced.
