+The strongest numerical result is scene rhythm: 34 marked breaks, 9.06 per 10,000 words and 915.2 words per scene all sit near target. The primary working measures also pass: sentence mean, long-sentence share and words per scene are all inside their adopted ranges. The clearest departure is distribution/readability: a standard deviation of 11.34 against about 26 and FRE 94.6 against 72.3 indicate prose that uses a narrower, plainer band than requested. Because mean, short-share and long-share already pass, a repair should not globally lengthen sentences or add difficult words. It should revise a small number of explanatory passages into clearer compound/complex hierarchies and slightly more exact vocabulary while protecting dialogue and landing beats.
